  "title": "Avoiding Liquidations: A Beginner’s Guide",
  "summary": "Getting liquidated is one of the roughest early experiences in futures trading, and one of the most common. It happens to nearly every trader at some point, usually before they’ve fully understood how leverage and margin interact. The good news is that liquidation is avoidable almost every time, once you know what actually causes it. […]",
